================================================================================
3. EVERYTHING ELSE — see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICE.md
================================================================================

Neither grant above applies to third-party material. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICE.md
enumerates every third-party item that remains in this package, names the rights
holder, states the basis on which it is included, and says what a re-user must do.
In particular, and without limiting that file:

  references/spec/cognitive_complexity_spec_rules.md
        is the author's paraphrase of the SonarSource Cognitive Complexity white
        paper v1.7 (Copyright SonarSource S.A., 2023, Switzerland; "All content
        is copyright protected") and of the RSPEC-3776 rule description, and is
        CC BY 4.0 as the author's own writing — except for the short quoted
        phrases it carries, which remain SonarSource's and are excluded from both
        grants above. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICE.md section 3 measures their extent.

  the Appendix C and Appendix A.3 cases inside experiments/microcorpus/
        are derived from the white paper's worked examples and, for Appendix C,
        from the upstream projects it names. Excluded from both grants above.
        See experiments/microcorpus/ATTRIBUTION.md.

  the analyzer messages and increment labels inside results/raw/microcorpus/sonar_*.json
  and the scanner logs results/raw/*/*/sonar.scanner.log and
  results/raw/microcorpus/sonar_*.scanner.log
        are emitted by SonarSource software and remain SonarSource's.

  the npm and PyPI metadata in reproduction/
        describes third-party packages that are not distributed here; each
        package is governed by its own licence when you install it.

  the subject repositories measured by this study
        are not distributed here at all. Re-obtain them at the commit SHAs in
        data/repos/manifest.csv, under each repository's own licence; several are
        non-commercial, source-available or copyleft (see data/repos/LICENSES.md).

If this file and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICE.md ever disagree about a path, the more
restrictive reading applies until the discrepancy is resolved.
